: "text", "content": ""}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn6le03ob02re2img05.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn6le03ob02re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn6le03ob02re2img05.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: OK, these onions are chopped. Is that enough?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Oh, thanks, Peter, but that's a bit too much.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: Alright, I will have to put some aside. Should I just saute them in the pan?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Oh, I've got to stir-fry the chicken, but you go ahead and use the saucepan."}, {"time": "15300", "image": "engenn6le03ob02re2img05.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: How much chicken do you need?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Oh, with that many people, we're going to need more than a pound.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: Do I stir in the 4 ounces of cream now?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: No, that's got to go in later after the chicken is cooked.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: Do I saute the red peppers too?"}, {"time": "29000", "image": "engenn6le03ob02re2img05.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: OK, you guys, you know what? I really appreciate all your help, but there are just too many cooks in this small kitchen. How about you guys just chill with a glass of wine?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: Alright. It's way more tasty when you cook it anyway.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: We can set the table.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Sounds great. I need to finish combining all the ingredients."}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "audio", "value": "engenn6le03ob02re6aud01"}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "text", "id": 2, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}]}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa: Dinner for Four"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Too Many Cooks"}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "scholar > Looking to the Stars > Florence Nightingale"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe routines and regular activities in a wider range of social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le03ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Too much or too many?"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use \"<span class=\"strong\">too much</span>\" or \"<span class=\"strong\">too many</span>\" to say that there is something in excess or to express that you don't like the situation.<br/>Use \"<span class=\"strong\">too much</span>\" with uncountable nouns.<br/> Use \"<span class=\"strong\">too many</span>\" with countable nouns."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Too much\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Too many\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Be careful! That salt is a bit <span class=\\\"strong\\\">too much</span>.<br/>You have drunk <span class=\\\"strong\\\">too much</span> wine!<br/>You are cooking <span class=\\\"strong\\\">too much</span> chicken.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">There are just <span class=\\\"strong\\\">too many</span> cooks in this small kitchen.<br/>There are <span class=\\\"strong\\\">too many</span> ounces of cream!<br/>More than 3 chicken legs is <span class=\\\"strong\\\">too many</span>.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We need a pound of chicken for 4 people."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Can you take the carton of cream out of the fridge?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " You need to do it!"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " \u201cHave got to\u201d is used to express necessity. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " \u201cHave got to\u201d has irregular forms in the past and future. Look at the chart below."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I've got  to</span>  start the vindaloo sauce.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I <span class=\\\"italic\\\">  had to</span> start the vindaloo sauce.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I <span class=\\\"italic\\\">will</span> have to start the vindaloo sauce.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I've got to</span> put some onions aside.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> had to</span> put some onions aside.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> will</span> have to put some onions aside.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to put aside"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to save or keep to be used at a later time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Peter will put aside the extra onions to be used at another time."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob02aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about cooking and dining."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "red pepper"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a sweet bell shaped pepper"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The red peppers also need to be sauteed before they're added to the curry."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob02aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tasty"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "describing food that tastes good"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Peter thinks Vanessa's cooking is always very tasty."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob02aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to set the table"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to set the place for each person at the dinner table with a fork, knife, glass, etc."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I can't cook, so I will help set the table."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob02aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to combine"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to put together or to mix"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The last step in making the curry is to combine all the ingredients together."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob02aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ingredient"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "one of the necessary food items or spice in making one dish"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: All of the ingredients have to be prepared right for the dish to taste good."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob02aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Decide with your partner on a meal you both know how to make."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue of 12 lines on how to prepare the meal."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write the quantities of the ingredients you need. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write the steps on how to prepare the meal."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice the dialogue together. Does it make sense?"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write a dialogue on how to prepare a meal."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I express quantity on the ingredients we need for a meal."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write the step on how to make a meal."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make sure the directions make sense."}]}]}